00:29:56.000 --> 00:30:01.000
♪

00:30:02.000 --> 00:30:04.000
With us, God,

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:08.000
when we walk through the valley of the shadow of death,

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:11.000
and when we stand on the mountaintop of joy,

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:14.000
God, we find you near.

00:30:14.000 --> 00:30:16.000
We find you close to us.

00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:19.000
In the breath of our lungs,

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:22.000
in the beat of our heart,

00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:24.000
in our skin, God,

00:30:24.000 --> 00:30:27.000
you are woven in and throughout,

00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:32.000
and we find you present in all things, God.

00:30:32.000 --> 00:30:38.000
I ask for your comfort where we're hurting.

00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:43.000
I ask for the bone of reconciliation

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:47.000
where things in our world are broken

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:50.000
and in need of saving, God.

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:54.000
Would we find you there?

00:30:55.000 --> 00:31:00.000
It's in your name that we ask all these things, God.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.000
Thank you guys for worshiping with us,

00:31:03.000 --> 00:31:09.000
and I just want to introduce to you guys Stephanie Acuna.

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:13.000
She is going to be doing our reading tonight before Brett's message.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.000
So without further ado, thank you, Stephanie,

00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:19.000
for sharing this time with us, and I'm going to pass it to you.

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:24.000
Thank you very much, and thank you for that beautiful music.

00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:28.000
Tonight our reading is going to be from the book of Luke,

00:31:28.000 --> 00:31:35.000
chapter 22, verses 47 through 53.

00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:37.000
This is about when Jesus was arrested.

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:40.000
While he was still speaking, a crowd came up,

00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:45.000
and the man who was called Judas, one of the 12, was leading them.

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.000
He approached Jesus to kiss him,

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:53.000
but Jesus asked him, Judas, are you betraying the son of man with a kiss?

00:31:53.000 --> 00:31:57.000
When Jesus' followers saw what was going to happen, they said,

00:31:57.000 --> 00:32:00.000
Lord, should we strike with our swords?

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:03.000
And one of them struck the servant of the high priest,

00:32:03.000 --> 00:32:05.000
cutting off his right ear.

00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:09.000
But Jesus answered, no more of this.

00:32:09.000 --> 00:32:12.000
And he touched the man's ear and healed him.

00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:15.000
Then Jesus said to the chief priests,

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:19.000
the officers of the temple guard and the elders would come for him.

00:32:19.000 --> 00:32:24.000
Am I leading a rebellion that you have come with swords and clubs?

00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:27.000
Every day I was with you in the temple courts,

00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:30.000
and you did not lay a hand on me.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:37.000
But this is your hour when darkness reigns.

00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:39.000
Thank you, Stephanie.

00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:41.000
Well, good evening, everyone.

00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:43.000
Grace and peace.

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:45.000
Welcome to the table.

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:48.000
And I'm just really, really grateful to be with you all.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:53.000
And you may have also noticed that we have little comments popping up.

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:57.000
So Sarah Johns is serving as our hostess tonight,

00:32:57.000 --> 00:33:02.000
and so she'll be also running kind of the official table Facebook account.

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:06.000
So if you see comments from the table, that will be Sarah.

00:33:06.000 --> 00:33:09.000
And so thank you, Sarah, for jumping into that role.

00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:12.000
We're trying to kind of create as much community as we can,

00:33:12.000 --> 00:33:15.000
even with this medium that we have here.

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:18.000
So I'm grateful for folks like Sarah who jump in

00:33:18.000 --> 00:33:21.000
and help us start to inch towards creating that.

00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:23.000
So, all right.

00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:27.000
We are, of course, in our series on the Gospel of Luke,

00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:34.000
where we're walking really just kind of front to back right through this gospel.

00:33:34.000 --> 00:33:36.000
And we are getting towards the end of the book.

00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:39.000
In fact, next week will be our last message in this series.

00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:45.000
But tonight, the title of my message is This Is Your Hour.

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:49.000
And our text is the one that Stephanie just read.

00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:54.000
That's kind of our primary one, Luke 22, verses 47 through 53.

00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:57.000
So I'm not going to reread that now,

00:33:57.000 --> 00:34:01.000
but if you're listening to this later on the podcast or something,

00:34:01.000 --> 00:34:04.000
you can go ahead and look that up and read it yourself.

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:09.000
So there's the line that just keeps sticking with me.

00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:12.000
It's Jesus' closing line where he says,

00:34:12.000 --> 00:34:17.000
This is your hour when darkness reigns.

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:21.000
And I think the reason I just can't get it out of my head,

00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:23.000
I just keep returning to it,

00:34:23.000 --> 00:34:33.000
is because I see him doing something that we in our culture kind of don't do well.

00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:39.000
We raised on the power of positive thinking.

00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:47.000
We who so often are just very tempted to turn a blind eye to the darkness in the world.

00:34:47.000 --> 00:34:53.000
We who have trouble facing our own pain, like much less the pain of others.

00:34:53.000 --> 00:34:59.000
We who would rather have the peace of a lie than the discomfort of a hard truth.

00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:03.000
We who believe that if we just had enough faith,

00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:07.000
well then no bad things would ever happen to us or anyone else.

00:35:07.000 --> 00:35:14.000
We who secretly are actually really struggling with the darkness in our own lives,

00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:19.000
but we continue to project outwardly that everything's fine.

00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:28.000
We who seem just bent on making people who are super sweet, nice Christians

00:35:28.000 --> 00:35:36.000
instead of really honest, real, and willing to love even when it hurts Christians.

00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:42.000
We who feel the need to defend God by pretending that there is no such thing as the darkness,

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:48.000
that the darkness really is only the light, seen from a different angle.

00:35:48.000 --> 00:35:53.000
Yeah, we could really use Jesus' perspective on this,

00:35:53.000 --> 00:35:56.000
because the truth is that he's having none of that.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.000
And so he just kind of comes out and says it.

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:03.000
Like, yep, I mean, whatever you want to call it, like Satan, the demonic, evil,

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:06.000
this is your hour.

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:08.000
This is your battle.

00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:10.000
This match goes to you.

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:13.000
Congrats. Live it up. Soak it up.

00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:15.000
Hope you enjoy it.

00:36:15.000 --> 00:36:21.000
And honestly, in a season that we're in right now of a pandemic,

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:26.000
of the ugliness of a police system that has sparred just for too long,

00:36:26.000 --> 00:36:29.000
often used its power in corrupt ways,

00:36:29.000 --> 00:36:34.000
in a world of men kneeling on other men's necks or shooting them in the back,

00:36:34.000 --> 00:36:38.000
in a time where we all wonder how long we'll have a job

00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:43.000
when our leaders seem intent on preserving their own image and ego

00:36:43.000 --> 00:36:46.000
over the good of the country in that kind of world,

00:36:46.000 --> 00:36:49.000
call me crazy, but I'm just going to go ahead and kind of admit,

00:36:49.000 --> 00:36:52.000
like, well, crap, evil, this is your hour.

00:36:52.000 --> 00:36:54.000
This is your battle.

00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:56.000
This match goes to you.

00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:58.000
Congrats. Live it up. Soak it up.

00:36:58.000 --> 00:36:59.000
Hope you enjoy it.

00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:07.000
Because, because it will not last.

00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:12.000
Christ does not mince words about the evil in this world.

00:37:12.000 --> 00:37:16.000
He does not try to spin stories about how the darkness is actually the light,

00:37:16.000 --> 00:37:18.000
just seeing it from a different perspective.

00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:25.000
No, he's very clear about the fallen, intragic nature of this world.

00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:31.000
And that's why he can say, this is your hour when the darkness reigns.

00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:34.000
I mean, even that word reigns.

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:40.000
But he can say that because the opening lines of chapter 24,

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:42.000
just two chapters later,

00:37:43.000 --> 00:37:46.000
tell this story.

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:50.000
On the first day of the week, very early in the morning,

00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:54.000
the women took the spices they had prepared and went to the tomb.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:58.000
They found the stone rolled away from the tomb.

00:37:58.000 --> 00:38:04.000
But when they entered, they did not find the body of the Lord Jesus.

00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:06.000
While they were wondering about this,

00:38:06.000 --> 00:38:12.000
suddenly two men in clothes that gleamed like lightning stood beside them.

00:38:12.000 --> 00:38:17.000
In their fright, the women bowed down with their faces to the ground.

00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:22.000
But the men said to them, why do you look for the living among the dead?

00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:26.000
He is not here. He has risen.

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:29.000
Remember how he told you while he was still with you in Galilee,

00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:32.000
the son of man must be delivered over to the hands of sinners,

00:38:32.000 --> 00:38:36.000
be crucified, and on the third day be raised again.

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:41.000
Then they remembered his words.

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:45.000
Now, I'm thinking that's a really key part to forget.

00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:49.000
Then, that's right, then they remembered his words.

00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:50.000
Like, how could they forget that?

00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.000
But you see, that's just it.

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:56.000
I think this is what suffering, pain, loss,

00:38:56.000 --> 00:38:58.000
I mean, it's what Karen named earlier, grief.

00:38:58.000 --> 00:39:00.000
This is what they do to us.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:05.000
They tell us, they speak a word, and that word is forever.

00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:08.000
The darkness says, whatever you're facing,

00:39:08.000 --> 00:39:11.000
like your marriage falling apart is forever.

00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:14.000
Your company falling apart is forever.

00:39:14.000 --> 00:39:17.000
Your bank account dwindling forever.

00:39:17.000 --> 00:39:20.000
Your depression and suicidal thoughts are forever.

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:23.000
Your nagging sense of failure is forever.

00:39:23.000 --> 00:39:25.000
Your aching loneliness is forever.

00:39:25.000 --> 00:39:28.000
The pandemic, the darkness says, is forever.

00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:32.000
Police brutality is forever.

00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:37.000
Even the raw wounds of coming out about your sexual orientation,

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:41.000
experiencing the rejection of others,

00:39:41.000 --> 00:39:44.000
even your church community, this is an experience, of course,

00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:47.000
that many in our community at the table have had.

00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:53.000
The darkness says, that is forever.

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:57.000
But that is the great lie.

00:39:57.000 --> 00:40:02.000
Which is why Jesus does not say, darkness, you win forever.

00:40:02.000 --> 00:40:08.000
What he says is, this is your hour.

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:13.000
In other words, this is your time.

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:16.000
This is your season.

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:20.000
But just as at the beginning of all things,

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:24.000
God looked at the sea and said,

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:29.000
your boundary line is here, but no further.

00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:32.000
Just as God looked at the mountains and said,

00:40:32.000 --> 00:40:35.000
you will go this far, but not one inch more.

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:39.000
So Jesus says, this will be your hour.

00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:43.000
Friday, crucifixion is your hour.

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:49.000
But Sunday, resurrection is my, is Christ's hour.

00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:53.000
This will not last forever.

00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:58.000
You see, the darkness is not the truest,

00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:01.000
the most real thing about the world.

00:41:01.000 --> 00:41:05.000
The light is the truest thing.

00:41:05.000 --> 00:41:08.000
The God we've come to know in Jesus,

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:15.000
the one who is himself endless, self-giving, self-emptying love,

00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:21.000
that he is the truest thing about the world.

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:24.000
In the beautiful words of Psalm 30 verse five,

00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:27.000
this is maybe for some people their life verse.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:35.000
Weeping may last for a night, but joy comes in the morning.

00:41:35.000 --> 00:41:40.000
I think that's a word over you, table lights.

00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:42.000
I don't know what you call y'all, friends of the table.

00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:44.000
Let me read it over you again.

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:51.000
Weeping may last for a night, but joy comes in the morning.

00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:59.000
What this is naming is that the weeping, the mourning, the grief is not forever.

00:41:59.000 --> 00:42:06.000
And as I reflect on the stories of people of faith in the Bible,

00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:13.000
this is a truth that I see just ring out again and again.

00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:21.000
I think of Joseph thrown into a pit by his brothers.

00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:26.000
You remember the story, only to later be falsely accused of a crime

00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:28.000
and then thrown into prison.

00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:31.000
I mean, talk about like the lowest of the low.

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:36.000
It's enough to be thrown into a pit by your brothers and then sold into slavery

00:42:36.000 --> 00:42:39.000
and then add on top of that like insult to injury,

00:42:39.000 --> 00:42:42.000
falsely accused of a crime, thrown into prison.

00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:43.000
Like it's a mess.

00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:50.000
And there he sits at midlife feeling like his life is, it's just over.

00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:52.000
But it was not the case.

00:42:52.000 --> 00:42:54.000
God had plans for Joseph.

00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:56.000
And just a few years later,

00:42:56.000 --> 00:43:02.000
he was second in command of the greatest empire in the known world.

00:43:02.000 --> 00:43:07.000
His suffering was not forever.

00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:15.000
I think of Hagar, purchased as a slave in Egypt, mistreated by her master Sarah,

00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:18.000
eventually dismissed by the family,

00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:23.000
and then unjustly driven into the wilderness with her young boy

00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:29.000
with nothing more than a little food and a small container of water.

00:43:29.000 --> 00:43:33.000
And, of course, those quickly run out.

00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:40.000
And eventually the little boy begins to cry from dehydration and she knows this is it.

00:43:40.000 --> 00:43:43.000
This is how it ends.

00:43:43.000 --> 00:43:47.000
And so she puts him under a little bush, the text says,

00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:50.000
and then she wanders a stone's throw away.

00:43:50.000 --> 00:43:51.000
Why?

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:57.000
Because she cannot bear to watch her son die.

00:43:57.000 --> 00:44:00.000
And the story goes that she began to sob.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:01.000
Why?

00:44:01.000 --> 00:44:04.000
Because she thought that moment was it.

00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:06.000
It was forever.

00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:10.000
It would be the thing that would define her.

00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:12.000
But no.

00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:15.000
An angel of the Lord appears and says,

00:44:15.000 --> 00:44:20.000
Do not be afraid, for God has heard your little boy crying.

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:22.000
Lift him up.

00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:24.000
Take him by the hand.

00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:25.000
And then a promise.

00:44:25.000 --> 00:44:29.000
For he will become a great nation.

00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:32.000
And that's exactly what happened.

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:36.000
Hagar's suffering was not forever.

00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:40.000
Or think of the apostle Paul, also known as Saul,

00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:44.000
who earlier in his life was persecuting Christians,

00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:50.000
watching as the first Christian martyr, Stephen, is stoned to death.

00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:52.000
He's there overseeing the whole thing.

00:44:52.000 --> 00:44:56.000
Because Paul, he is zealous for the ways of his forefathers.

00:44:56.000 --> 00:44:59.000
He is ready to stand for the truth.

00:44:59.000 --> 00:45:03.000
And so he travels around attempting to stamp out this Christian heresy

00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:08.000
when suddenly on the road to Damascus a light shines around him

00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:11.000
and a voice from heaven speaks to him saying,

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:16.000
Saul, Saul, why do you persecute me?

00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:18.000
And he says, Who are you?

00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:24.000
And the voice says, I am Jesus, who you persecute.

00:45:24.000 --> 00:45:30.000
And in that moment, Paul realizes that he,

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:37.000
who was so zealous for God, has actually been fighting God.

00:45:37.000 --> 00:45:41.000
That he who was so passionate for the ways of the Spirit

00:45:41.000 --> 00:45:44.000
has been opposing the Holy Spirit.

00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:50.000
In that God moment, it's so powerful that Paul literally falls off his horse

00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:55.000
and when he opens up his eyes, he is completely blind.

00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:59.000
And all the voice says is, Get up, go into the city,

00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:03.000
and you will be told what to do.

00:46:03.000 --> 00:46:05.000
And the story goes that he was led into the city,

00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:13.000
and for three days he was blind, and he ate and drank nothing.

00:46:13.000 --> 00:46:17.000
Is that the image of a happy person, a faith-filled person?

00:46:17.000 --> 00:46:18.000
No.

00:46:18.000 --> 00:46:23.000
Paul is in the darkness, both literally and figuratively.

00:46:23.000 --> 00:46:28.000
And I'm sure he thought, what, it would be forever.

00:46:28.000 --> 00:46:32.000
He probably assumed that this is it for me.

00:46:32.000 --> 00:46:34.000
This is the end of my journey.

00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:39.000
But little did he know that what looked like the end of his story

00:46:39.000 --> 00:46:45.000
was actually the beginning of the best years of his life.

00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:47.000
That he would recover his sight,

00:46:47.000 --> 00:46:50.000
and in fact, he would then go on to write letters

00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:53.000
that now make up two-thirds of the New Testament,

00:46:53.000 --> 00:46:55.000
some of you holding your hands right now.

00:46:55.000 --> 00:46:59.000
And to this day, those texts are read and reread and memorized

00:46:59.000 --> 00:47:08.000
and cherished by billions of people all over the world.

00:47:08.000 --> 00:47:14.000
And at the risk of putting us on the same level as Joseph, Hagar, and Paul,

00:47:14.000 --> 00:47:18.000
I also think of some people at a little church in Sachse, Texas,

00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:21.000
that launched out in November of 2019,

00:47:21.000 --> 00:47:25.000
and then just four months later got blindsided by a pandemic

00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:28.000
we haven't seen the likes of in a hundred years.

00:47:28.000 --> 00:47:31.000
And now we're five and a half months into a quarantine,

00:47:31.000 --> 00:47:35.000
and there's a lot of days that it looks really, really bleak out there.

00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:38.000
We're tired, more than a little depressed.

00:47:38.000 --> 00:47:40.000
It's hard right now.

00:47:41.000 --> 00:47:44.000
But Jesus' words to us are,

00:47:44.000 --> 00:47:48.000
the darkness will have its hour,

00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:51.000
but morning is coming.

00:47:51.000 --> 00:47:55.000
Resurrection is on its way.

00:47:55.000 --> 00:47:59.000
So remain faithful, and you will look back years from now

00:47:59.000 --> 00:48:08.000
and be astonished at what God will do in and through you in this season.

00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:10.000
Let me pray for you.

00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:14.000
Lord Jesus,

00:48:14.000 --> 00:48:19.000
we receive this as your word to us.

00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:22.000
God, I lift up every person who, just right now,

00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:26.000
they're in a place where the darkness feels like forever,

00:48:26.000 --> 00:48:30.000
or for those who have been there really recently.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:33.000
And I speak over them your truth,

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:35.000
that it's not forever.

00:48:35.000 --> 00:48:38.000
Darkness has its hour, but the light is coming.

00:48:38.000 --> 00:48:40.000
Hope is coming.

00:48:40.000 --> 00:48:44.000
Christ, your love is present and available to us,

00:48:44.000 --> 00:48:46.000
and you can meet us even today.

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:51.000
We can have a taste of that resurrection life and hope and love even today.

00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:55.000
And so, God, we receive it.

00:48:55.000 --> 00:48:58.000
So where there's discouragement,

00:48:58.000 --> 00:49:02.000
God, I pray hope.

00:49:02.000 --> 00:49:05.000
Where there's a sense of despair,

00:49:05.000 --> 00:49:09.000
I pray for community, connection, and love.

00:49:09.000 --> 00:49:14.000
Where there's just a sense of distance from you, God,

00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:15.000
may you close the gap.

00:49:15.000 --> 00:49:22.000
May your spirit right now begin to speak to people.

00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:24.000
Be near us, God.

00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:27.000
Carry us.

00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:30.000
And we trust that though the weeping lasts for a night,

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:33.000
God, your joy is coming.

00:49:33.000 --> 00:49:40.000
In the powerful, life-changing resurrection name of Jesus, I pray.

00:49:40.000 --> 00:49:42.000
Amen.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:05.000
I will not break your heart, but dismiss your fears.

00:50:05.000 --> 00:50:11.000
Get over your hill and see what you find there.

00:50:11.000 --> 00:50:18.000
With grace in your heart and flowers in your hair,

00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:22.000
there will come a time you'll see.

00:50:22.000 --> 00:50:25.000
With no more tears in love,

00:50:25.000 --> 00:50:30.000
I will not break your heart, but dismiss your fears.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:36.000
Get over your hill and see what you find there.

00:50:36.000 --> 00:50:43.000
With grace in your heart and flowers in your hair,

